proof.text:
We make the tensor identifications used in the comparison explicit. Use the inverses of the bifunctorial comparisons $\mu^u$ of [lem-kun-inverse-image-monoidal] to distribute every inverse image over a derived tensor. Use the specific comparisons $\gamma$ constructed in [def-kun-kunneth-map] by the canonical module-linear sheaf composition maps, applied termwise and descended to the unbounded derived categories, to use $rh=s$ and $qh=jp$. Their module structures and composite-adjunction normalization are part of the current definition; the following calculation concerns these maps. In particular, put $D=P\otimes_A^{\mathbf L}B$, let $\rho=\gamma_{r,h}^{-1}:h^{-1}r^{-1}\to s^{-1}$, and let $\sigma=\gamma_{j,p}\circ\gamma_{q,h}^{-1}:h^{-1}q^{-1}\to p^{-1}j^{-1}$. The exact coherence equality needed below is
$$
\begin{aligned}
 &(\rho_{a^{-1}P}\otimes\sigma_{b^{-1}B})
 \circ(\mu^h_{r^{-1}a^{-1}P,q^{-1}b^{-1}B})^{-1}
 \circ h^{-1}(t_Z)\circ\gamma_{d,h,D}\\
 &\qquad=(1_{s^{-1}a^{-1}P}\otimes p^{-1}\gamma_{b,j,B})\circ t_W(P,B),
\end{aligned}
$$
where both sides go from $e^{-1}D$ to $s^{-1}a^{-1}P\otimes_A^{\mathbf L}p^{-1}j^{-1}b^{-1}B$. The comparisons also commute with the unit maps $u_Z,u_W$. This equality follows by applying the tensor-composition equation of [lem-kun-derived-pullback-composition-monoidal] to $(d,h)$ and then its associativity equation to $(a,r,h)$, $(b,q,h)$ and $(b,j,p)$, using $rh=s$, $qh=jp$ and $bj=c$; the last instance gives $\gamma_{j,p,b^{-1}B}\circ\gamma_{b,jp,B}=p^{-1}\gamma_{b,j,B}\circ\gamma_{c,p,B}$. The unit-compatibility clause gives compatibility with $u_Z,u_W$. No symmetry is used.
